# Code generated by Claude
"""Flat configuration dictionaries for the beaker-on-hotplate task (models/scenes/chemistry_lab_beaker_hotplate.xml).

Every pose and threshold of the task lives here so a later run can randomize it by copying a dict and
changing entries (task_beaker_hotplate.apply_task_poses() writes the object poses into the model).
Plain dicts of numbers, strings and tuples; no nesting, no classes. This module has no functions.

The dictionaries and who reads them:
    TASK_CFG: scene file, object and robot poses and the start-up times of the task, read by src/task_beaker_hotplate.py,
        src/staging_source.py and src/task_policy.py (a recorded run stores its own copy, which src/replay.py uses). The staging, ready and grasp poses were found by the layout
        search and must be re-computed (experiments/beaker_hotplate_layout_search.py) if the objects, spawn or pedestal change.
    BEAKER_CFG: the hollow glass beaker (size, wall, masses, contact friction of the fingers), built at load time by src/beaker.py.
    GRIP_FORCE_TABLE: the gripper force cap per object, looked up by the demo generator and later the openpi adapter.
    FURNITURE_CFG: the layered furniture map (design plan §3.4; src/furniture_map.py): resolution, the two height layers and the clearances of the first approximation.
    STANCE_CFG: settings of the stance finder (src/stance_finder.py).
    GRASP_MAP_CFG: build settings of the grasp reachability map (design plan §3.1; src/grasp_rules.py, src/reach_map.py). Map files are not committed, only these settings.
    SEARCH_CFG: settings of the offline staging pose search (experiments/beaker_hotplate_staging_search.py).
    LAYOUT_CFG: settings of the joint layout and staging search with slack at every task pose
        (experiments/beaker_hotplate_layout_search.py).
    STAGING_CFG: speeds, ramps, tolerances and time limits of the scripted staging source (src/staging_source.py).
    EPISODE_CFG: time limits, the 2 s after a success, logging rate and spawn height of the episode runner (src/episode_runner.py).
    SUCCESS_CFG: site, geom and body names and tolerances of the success check (task_beaker_hotplate.check_success()).
Entries marked NEW in the comments of STAGING_CFG were chosen recently and are not yet approved. All numbers are choices for this
simulation, not measurements of the real hardware.

Staging sequence (built in src/staging_source.py from STAGING_CFG): DRIVE to the staging pose -> PEDESTAL to pedestal_q ->
ARMS (both arms) to the home pose -> NECK frames the beaker, the hotplate and both grippers -> HANDOFF (the vision-language-action (VLA) policy takes over the arm from here).
The base and the arms never move at the same time.

World frame: the bench is centred on the origin (top z = 0.96, x +-2.2, y +-0.8). The robot faces its own
+x. The staging pose is on the +y side of the bench, facing -y (yaw = -90 deg).
"""

